		{
			"id": "Kn6GfURy",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 6530,
			"y": 1145,
			"width": 436.25970458984375,
			"height": 125,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bD0F",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1993971380,
			"version": 2,
			"versionNonce": 795116537,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795063059456,
			"created": 1795063059456,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "PaymentService (external)\n- Own payment status + transaction details\n- Core Banking prevents overdraft atomically\n- Save final outcome + outbox in same TX\n- No remote RPC inside LimitService TX",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"baseFontSize": null,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "PaymentService (external)\n- Own payment status + transaction details\n- Core Banking prevents overdraft atomically\n- Save final outcome + outbox in same TX\n- No remote RPC inside LimitService TX",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"labelPosition": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "K9COvVIa",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 6530,
			"y": 1455,
			"width": 486.5997009277344,
			"height": 225,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bD0G",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 783588601,
			"version": 2,
			"versionNonce": 272032449,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795063059456,
			"created": 1795063059456,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Saga + Compensation (async)\n1) Payment failed -> outbox event\n2) CDC -> Kafka -> RollbackWorker\n3) Release once, then commit offset\n4) Success -> confirm reservation\n\nKafka gives durable replay / buffering\nCDC reads DB change log (not powered by Kafka)\nAlternative : outbox polling for simpler setup",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"baseFontSize": null,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Saga + Compensation (async)\n1) Payment failed -> outbox event\n2) CDC -> Kafka -> RollbackWorker\n3) Release once, then commit offset\n4) Success -> confirm reservation\n\nKafka gives durable replay / buffering\nCDC reads DB change log (not powered by Kafka)\nAlternative : outbox polling for simpler setup",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"labelPosition": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "ugq2Two0",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 6530,
			"y": 1840,
			"width": 410.87969970703125,
			"height": 175,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bD0H",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 732201726,
			"version": 2,
			"versionNonce": 2112490396,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795063059456,
			"created": 1795063059456,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "ProcessedEvent (consumer dedupe)\n- eventID UNIQUE\n- paymentID\n- processed_at\n\nReservation state also prevents duplicate\nrelease across different event IDs",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"baseFontSize": null,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "ProcessedEvent (consumer dedupe)\n- eventID UNIQUE\n- paymentID\n- processed_at\n\nReservation state also prevents duplicate\nrelease across different event IDs",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"labelPosition": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "bVK7wBrY",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 4243,
			"y": 2180,
			"width": 566.11962890625,
			"height": 300,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bD0I",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1943347853,
			"version": 2,
			"versionNonce": 248154764,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795063059456,
			"created": 1795063059456,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Security / Monitoring / Testing\n- API Gateway authN, authZ, rate limiting\n- Biometric / step-up auth for limit changes (upstream)\n- TLS / mTLS for gRPC, encryption at rest\n- Validate trusted userId + paymentId ownership\n- TraceID / requestID (OpenTelemetry), no sensitive logs\n- Monitor p99, error rate, approval vs rejection rate\n- DB lock wait / CPU / I/O, pool usage\n- Kafka lag, stuck reservations, outbox age\n- Load test at peak 2000 QPS + hot user contention\n- Test duplicate / timeout / crash / midnight / recovery\n- Rolling deploy + backward-compatible DB migrations",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"baseFontSize": null,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Security / Monitoring / Testing\n- API Gateway authN, authZ, rate limiting\n- Biometric / step-up auth for limit changes (upstream)\n- TLS / mTLS for gRPC, encryption at rest\n- Validate trusted userId + paymentId ownership\n- TraceID / requestID (OpenTelemetry), no sensitive logs\n- Monitor p99, error rate, approval vs rejection rate\n- DB lock wait / CPU / I/O, pool usage\n- Kafka lag, stuck reservations, outbox age\n- Load test at peak 2000 QPS + hot user contention\n- Test duplicate / timeout / crash / midnight / recovery\n- Rolling deploy + backward-compatible DB migrations",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"labelPosition": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "z1vMTXdi",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 4970,
			"y": 2240,
			"width": 504.5196838378906,
			"height": 500,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bD0J",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 418743922,
			"version": 2,
			"versionNonce": 870861698,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795063059456,
			"created": 1795063059456,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Deep Dive 1 : Check Limit (sync)\n1) Fetch trusted payment details outside DB TX\n2) BEGIN -> check idempotency (unique paymentId)\n3) Read + protect config (FOR SHARE)\n4) Create DailyUsage for MYT date if not exists\n    INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING\n5) Atomic conditional UPDATE (or short row lock)\n6) Persist reservation + decision in same TX\n7) COMMIT -> return approval / rejection\n\nSQL (conceptual)\nUPDATE daily_usage\nSET used_amount = used_amount + :amount\nWHERE user_id = :userId AND starts_at = :date\n  AND used_amount + :amount <= :dailyLimit\nRETURNING used_amount;\n0 rows -> reject (after daily row initialization)\n\nDaily usage + ReservationRecord = all or nothing\nDo NOT persist reservation asynchronously.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"baseFontSize": null,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Deep Dive 1 : Check Limit (sync)\n1) Fetch trusted payment details outside DB TX\n2) BEGIN -> check idempotency (unique paymentId)\n3) Read + protect config (FOR SHARE)\n4) Create DailyUsage for MYT date if not exists\n    INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING\n5) Atomic conditional UPDATE (or short row lock)\n6) Persist reservation + decision in same TX\n7) COMMIT -> return approval / rejection\n\nSQL (conceptual)\nUPDATE daily_usage\nSET used_amount = used_amount + :amount\nWHERE user_id = :userId AND starts_at = :date\n  AND used_amount + :amount <= :dailyLimit\nRETURNING used_amount;\n0 rows -> reject (after daily row initialization)\n\nDaily usage + ReservationRecord = all or nothing\nDo NOT persist reservation asynchronously.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"labelPosition": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "9oyh47DG",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 5640,
			"y": 2240,
			"width": 500.25970458984375,
			"height": 475,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bD0K",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 2067799339,
			"version": 2,
			"versionNonce": 651753868,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795063059456,
			"created": 1795063059456,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Deep Dive 2 : Failures / Recovery\n1) CheckLimit timeout after commit\n    -> retry same paymentId, return saved decision\n2) Payment fails -> Saga compensation\n    -> release only if status = RESERVED\n3) Consumer crash before Kafka offset commit\n    -> event replay; dedupe in same DB TX\n4) Payment outcome missing / expired\n    -> reconcile with authoritative payment status\n    -> unknown / unavailable: keep RESERVED\n5) Midnight -> new daily row, no reset scheduler\n    -> rollback against original usageDate\n\nRelease TX :\nBEGIN -> dedupe event + conditional state change\n-> decrement original day usedAmount once\n-> COMMIT -> commit Kafka offset\nConfirm TX : RESERVED -> CONFIRMED\n(no extra daily usage deduction)",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"baseFontSize": null,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Deep Dive 2 : Failures / Recovery\n1) CheckLimit timeout after commit\n    -> retry same paymentId, return saved decision\n2) Payment fails -> Saga compensation\n    -> release only if status = RESERVED\n3) Consumer crash before Kafka offset commit\n    -> event replay; dedupe in same DB TX\n4) Payment outcome missing / expired\n    -> reconcile with authoritative payment status\n    -> unknown / unavailable: keep RESERVED\n5) Midnight -> new daily row, no reset scheduler\n    -> rollback against original usageDate\n\nRelease TX :\nBEGIN -> dedupe event + conditional state change\n-> decrement original day usedAmount once\n-> COMMIT -> commit Kafka offset\nConfirm TX : RESERVED -> CONFIRMED\n(no extra daily usage deduction)",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"labelPosition": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "8Z6vE6qP",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 6300,
			"y": 2240,
			"width": 512.3196411132812,
			"height": 425,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bD0L",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 652927768,
			"version": 2,
			"versionNonce": 902246400,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795063059456,
			"created": 1795063059456,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Deep Dive 3 : Scalability / Trade-off\n- Start simple : 1 Postgres primary + replicas (HA)\n- Strong consistency : primary for authorization\n- Connection pool + short transactions\n- Conditional update avoids extra round trips\n- Optimistic lock : good for low contention\n    high contention -> many retries / high p99\n- Pessimistic lock : wait time on hot daily row\n- Shard by userID only when primary saturates\n    + aggregate write throughput\n    - higher cost / complexity\n    - does not fix hot user row\n- No Redis for authoritative balance / usage\n\nLimit change : serialize config update vs reserve\nLower limit below usedAmount -> block new transfers\nExisting reservations remain valid.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"baseFontSize": null,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Deep Dive 3 : Scalability / Trade-off\n- Start simple : 1 Postgres primary + replicas (HA)\n- Strong consistency : primary for authorization\n- Connection pool + short transactions\n- Conditional update avoids extra round trips\n- Optimistic lock : good for low contention\n    high contention -> many retries / high p99\n- Pessimistic lock : wait time on hot daily row\n- Shard by userID only when primary saturates\n    + aggregate write throughput\n    - higher cost / complexity\n    - does not fix hot user row\n- No Redis for authoritative balance / usage\n\nLimit change : serialize config update vs reserve\nLower limit below usedAmount -> block new transfers\nExisting reservations remain valid.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"labelPosition": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		}
	],
